  <p>
    <strong>Key Takeaway:</strong> "Zero gravity" is a misnomer—microgravity is more accurate. Weightlessness
    in orbit results from continuous free fall, not absence of gravity. Understanding microgravity is crucial
    for space exploration, affecting everything from human health to physics experiments to engineering design
    for future missions.
  </p>
